The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series. '''Warzone''' was announced as part of the line-up on January 21, 2026.<ref name="EWC WZ">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/1858963461054546414|title=@CallofDuty #Warzone drops back into Riyadh for #EWC2026|date=2024-11-20|author=Esports World Cup|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref> In 2026, Warzone will now be a Championship Finale event of an [[Activision]] organized circuit, the Warzone Resurgence Series.
:''See [https://liquipedia.net/esports/Esports_World_Cup/2026 here] to read about the Esports World Cup 2026, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

==Format==
<big>'''''All matches are played on Resurgence.</big>
* '''Group Stage'''
** 32 teams split into 2 groups of 16 teams
** Each group played 12 matches
** Top 5 from each group advances to Finals
** 6th-13th from each group proceed to Survival
* '''Survival'''
** 10 matches
** Top 6 advances to Finals
* '''Finals'''
** '''Match Point format'''
*** There is no match limit in the Finals.
*** There is no limit to number of teams who can be '''"Match Point Eligible"'''.
*** Once a team reaches '''150''' points, That team gained '''Match Point''' status from the next match onwards.
*** The first team under the '''"Match Point"''' status to win a match will be declared the 2026 Resurgence Series Champions.''
** After the winner/champion is declared, the rest of the standings are determined through points

